@director "Auggie Prine (as 'A. Prine'), (as 'Alan Smithee'), (as 'The Estate Of Auggie Prine')"

::cast
DELPHINE | Delphine Voss | heiress, eighth of her line, tenth of her name
CRUZ | Cruz Mandible | licensed reclamation technician, unlicensed romantic
SUPER | The Building | a voice in the ceiling
GRETA | Greta Voss-Voss | Delphine's sister, previously deceased, currently not
::endcast

LETTERBOX on

FADE in 2

SLUG SOLENNE RESIDENCES, FLOOR THIRTY | LATE, AND GETTING LATER

The city turns past the glass like something on a spit. Rain, but expensive rain.

3s

ACT 1 — Previously, On Hard Wired

NARRATOR:
Previously: Cruz fixed the boiler. Then he fixed the OTHER boiler. Then Greta died in a
freight elevator, which we are contractually obliged to remind you was NOT Cruz's fault.

NARRATOR:
Also, there was a war. It was mostly off-screen. Budget.

4s

SHOT
A doorbell chimes in a key chosen by a committee. DELPHINE VOSS crosses forty feet of
apartment in a robe that cost more than the door.
SHOT_END

DELPHINE:
Who is it.

CRUZ:
Building maintenance, ma'am. I'm here about your pressure.

DELPHINE:
My what.

CRUZ:
Your water pressure.

DELPHINE:
...Yes. Of course. That.

3s

SHOT
She opens the door. CRUZ MANDIBLE stands there holding a wrench the size of an argument.
He is wet. It is not raining in the corridor. Nobody addresses this.
SHOT_END

CRUZ:
I understand there's been some trouble with the flow.

DELPHINE:
It comes on strong and then it just... stops.

CRUZ:
That's a common fault in a unit this old.

DELPHINE:
The unit is four years old.

CRUZ:
Then it's a common fault in a unit this new.

2s

SHOT
CRUZ kneels at the wall panel. His overalls do the thing overalls do in this genre. The
camera holds on it for eleven seconds, which is four seconds longer than the director
remembers approving.
SHOT_END

4s

DELPHINE:
Will you have to go deep?

CRUZ:
Ma'am, I always go deep. It's in the manual.

SUPER:
RESIDENT ADVISORY. AN UNSCHEDULED MAINTENANCE EVENT IS OCCURRING IN YOUR UNIT.

DELPHINE:
Not now, building.

SUPER:
PLEASE RATE YOUR MAINTENANCE EVENT FROM ONE TO FIVE STARS.

CRUZ:
I said NOT NOW, building.

3s

ACT 2 — The Ductwork

OVERLAY
BITTERSWEET OPTICS PRESENTS

A FILM SHOT ENTIRELY IN ONE APARTMENT

BECAUSE WE ONLY HAD THE ONE APARTMENT
OVERLAY_END

3s

SHOT
CRUZ removes a grille. Steam rolls out of the duct in a great voluptuous cloud, because
the effects department owned exactly one machine and had been saving it.
SHOT_END

CRUZ:
Whoever installed this ran the hot line straight into the cold return. Cross-connected.
Everything's been touching everything for years.

DELPHINE:
In this building? Scandalous.

CRUZ:
I'll need to get my hands on the coupling.

DELPHINE:
Do you need help?

CRUZ:
I'd never turn down another pair of hands.

3s

SHOT
They both reach into the wall. Their fingers meet somewhere in the dark on a fitting neither
of them can see. There is a long, meaningful silence. Somewhere, a pipe groans.
SHOT_END

DELPHINE:
Is that —

CRUZ:
That's the ballcock.

DELPHINE:
The what?

CRUZ:
It's a technical term. It regulates the rise.

DELPHINE:
Of course it does.

4s

MUSIC
A saxophone begins, uninvited, from somewhere below the floor. It will not stop for the
remainder of the picture. The composer was paid in full.
MUSIC_END

SHOT
DELPHINE lets the robe slip from one shoulder, which is as far as it gets, because the
shoulder is where our exhibition licence expires.
SHOT_END

FADE out 3

NARRATOR:
What follows is forty minutes of the most explicit, most athletically ill-advised plumbing
in the history of the Basin. We are legally unable to show you any of it.

NARRATOR:
Instead, please enjoy this exterior shot of the building.

6s

SHOT
An exterior shot of the building. Nothing happens. A light in one window goes out. Another
goes on. A third window, unrelated, is simply a window.
SHOT_END

6s

SHOT
Still the exterior of the building. A bird lands. The bird leaves. The saxophone continues
without visible support.
SHOT_END

5s

INTERMISSION 20

FADE in 2

ACT 3 — Complications

SLUG THE SAME APARTMENT | FORTY MINUTES OF PLUMBING LATER

SHOT
CRUZ lies on the floor among his tools, spent, glowing, holding a length of copper pipe he
has plainly bent by hand. DELPHINE stands at the glass. Something enormous has been resolved.
SHOT_END

DELPHINE:
That was... comprehensive.

CRUZ:
I'll send the invoice.

DELPHINE:
Send it slowly.

3s

SHOT
The door opens. GRETA VOSS-VOSS stands in it. She is dressed for a funeral. Her own, as it
happens. She was buried in this.
SHOT_END

GRETA:
Hello, sister.

DELPHINE:
Greta! You're — you were in the elevator —

GRETA:
I got out at a different floor.

CRUZ:
That's not how elevators —

GRETA:
It's how THAT one works, Cruz.

4s

DELPHINE:
Why are you here?

GRETA:
Because the pressure's off in MY unit too.

3s

SHOT
CRUZ slowly sits up. He looks at his wrench. He looks at the two women. He looks at the
ceiling, where the building is definitely listening. He is a professional, and this is a
service call, and there is a form for this.
SHOT_END

CRUZ:
...I'll have to see the manifold.

SUPER:
RESIDENT ADVISORY. AN UNSCHEDULED MAINTENANCE EVENT IS OCCURRING IN YOUR UNIT.

SUPER:
AGAIN.

DELPHINE:
Building, mute.

SUPER:
MUTING. ENJOY YOUR MAINTENANCE EVENT. PLEASE RATE —

2s

FADE out 4

NARRATOR:
Hard Wired will return in "Hard Wired 5: Backflow Prevention", assuming the Estate of Auggie
Prine can be reached, which it cannot.

3s

